{"parentUuid":"71c16390-9020-4f8a-9619-16a9257d0e85","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgNmvHdeLwv6aZPzEuJgi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XByBBqzRVsCBsToADWuA8a","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"pinwiki WPC repair coil locked on at power up shorted transistor power driver board","mode":"standard"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21100,"cache_read_input_tokens":60284,"output_tokens":561,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":191},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21100,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":561,"cache_read_input_tokens":60284,"cache_creation_input_tokens":21100,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":21100},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XByBBqzRVsCBsToADWuA8a":{"query":"pinwiki WPC repair coil locked on at power up shorted transistor power driver board","mode":"standard"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ba79a434-fa96-4866-9e1b-f80179e2f271","apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CgNmvGr1ofCGvx8K7rxc3","requestRef":"881d8440-905a-4b09-8975-a2ed2155ee16","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"superpowers:systematic-debugging","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"283c4436-d09e-46c1-b338-4cc03eac9fc5","timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:11:29.556Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"71c16390-9020-4f8a-9619-16a9257d0e85","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"998498a1-a27e-413b-add6-ea4b12d88e02","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016gbEbxNmrx6SBQSwDrZRTN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"WPC power driver board A-12697 schematic fuse F103 solenoid 50V TIP36C TIP102\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Leon Borre Williams WPC and WPC-95 Driver Board Repair\",\"url\":\"https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/Leon_Borre_Williams_WPC_and_WPC-95_Driver_Board_Repair\"},{\"title\":\"Page 32 - WilliamsMidway WPC 91 Schematics 16-9289\",\"url\":\"https://planetarypinball.com/reference/partsmanuals/WMS_Schematic_WPC_16-9289/files/assets/seo/page32.html\"},{\"title\":\"WPC Power Driver Board - Replacement A-12697\",\"url\":\"https://www.planetarypinball.com/pinball-A-12697-TH\"},{\"title\":\"Power driver board – A-12697-x\",\"url\":\"https://www.pinball.co.uk/spares-accessories/power-driver-board-a-12697-x/\"},{\"title\":\"Power driver board – A-12697-x\",\"url\":\"https://www.pinball.co.uk/?p=35753\"},{\"title\":\"WPC89 Power Driver PCB Assy A-12697 (-1, -2, -3, -4)\",\"url\":\"https://www.planetarypinball.com/pinball-A-12697\"},{\"title\":\"WPC PDA12697X\",\"url\":\"https://www.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/WPC-PDA12697X\"},{\"title\":\"A 12697 1 3 4 WDB089 Bally Williams WPC89 WPC S Driver Board Pinball Machine  155239635245\",\"url\":\"https://napoleonexhibit.com/store/A-12697-1-3-4-WDB089-Bally-Williams-WPC89-WPC-S-Driver-Board-Pinball-Machine-_155239635245.html\"},{\"title\":\"Page 33 - Williams GREEN Parts Catalog 16-9932\",\"url\":\"https://www.planetarypinball.com/reference/partsmanuals/WMS_Parts_Green_16-9932/files/assets/seo/page33.html\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the board's general role and some background on the transistors, but nothing specific about fuse F103.\n\n- **Board function:** A Williams reference manual says the A-12697 power driver board handles the lamp, flipper, and solenoid circuits and supplies the +50V rail for solenoids, alongside +18V for lamps, +5V for logic, and +12V for switches. It contains no game-specific components, so it can be moved between games.\n- **Solenoid circuit troubleshooting:** A guide on the Pinwiki site describes tracing faulty high-current solenoid outputs through pre-driver, driver, and power transistor stages using the schematic and a test LED strip. It doesn't name F103 specifically.\n- **TIP102 and TIP36C:** A PinLED product page says the original design used TIP 102, 107, and 36C transistors, which become very hot in operation. That is the vendor's marketing claim, and its replacement uses MOSFETs instead.\n- **Fuses:** The PinLED page notes that its board includes LEDs to monitor the solenoid fuses and prints the fuse values on the layout. This suggests the fuse values are documented on the replacement board's silkscreen, not necessarily on the original schematic.\n- **Schematics:** The Williams parts catalog says schematics for these boards are in the operation manuals, not in the parts lists.\n\nI didn't find the schematic itself, the F103 fuse rating, or a confirmed TIP36C/TIP102 location on the A-12697. For those, the Williams WPC operation/service manual or the Pinwiki schematic images are the next places to check.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"edce167d-9cd8-4856-9092-b9f02b01e5d0","timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:11:36.590Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"WPC power driver board A-12697 schematic fuse F103 solenoid 50V TIP36C TIP102","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01VdmLewd8rggcZ1tsWjdXzn","content":[{"title":"Leon Borre Williams WPC and WPC-95 Driver Board Repair","url":"https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/Leon_Borre_Williams_WPC_and_WPC-95_Driver_Board_Repair"},{"title":"Page 32 - WilliamsMidway WPC 91 Schematics 16-9289","url":"https://planetarypinball.com/reference/partsmanuals/WMS_Schematic_WPC_16-9289/files/assets/seo/page32.html"},{"title":"WPC Power Driver Board - Replacement A-12697","url":"https://www.planetarypinball.com/pinball-A-12697-TH"},{"title":"Power driver board – A-12697-x","url":"https://www.pinball.co.uk/spares-accessories/power-driver-board-a-12697-x/"},{"title":"Power driver board – A-12697-x","url":"https://www.pinball.co.uk/?p=35753"},{"title":"WPC89 Power Driver PCB Assy A-12697 (-1, -2, -3, -4)","url":"https://www.planetarypinball.com/pinball-A-12697"},{"title":"WPC PDA12697X","url":"https://www.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/WPC-PDA12697X"},{"title":"A 12697 1 3 4 WDB089 Bally Williams WPC89 WPC S Driver Board Pinball Machine  155239635245","url":"https://napoleonexhibit.com/store/A-12697-1-3-4-WDB089-Bally-Williams-WPC89-WPC-S-Driver-Board-Pinball-Machine-_155239635245.html"},{"title":"Page 33 - Williams GREEN Parts Catalog 16-9932","url":"https://www.planetarypinball.com/reference/partsmanuals/WMS_Parts_Green_16-9932/files/assets/seo/page33.html"}]},"The search turned up the board's general role and some background on the transistors, but nothing specific about fuse F103.\n\n- **Board function:** A Williams reference manual says the A-12697 power driver board handles the lamp, flipper, and solenoid circuits and supplies the +50V rail for solenoids, alongside +18V for lamps, +5V for logic, and +12V for switches. It contains no game-specific components, so it can be moved between games.\n- **Solenoid circuit troubleshooting:** A guide on the Pinwiki site describes tracing faulty high-current solenoid outputs through pre-driver, driver, and power transistor stages using the schematic and a test LED strip. It doesn't name F103 specifically.\n- **TIP102 and TIP36C:** A PinLED product page says the original design used TIP 102, 107, and 36C transistors, which become very hot in operation. That is the vendor's marketing claim, and its replacement uses MOSFETs instead.\n- **Fuses:** The PinLED page notes that its board includes LEDs to monitor the solenoid fuses and prints the fuse values on the layout. This suggests the fuse values are documented on the replacement board's silkscreen, not necessarily on the original schematic.\n- **Schematics:** The Williams parts catalog says schematics for these boards are in the operation manuals, not in the parts lists.\n\nI didn't find the schematic itself, the F103 fuse rating, or a confirmed TIP36C/TIP102 location on the A-12697. For those, the Williams WPC operation/service manual or the Pinwiki schematic images are the next places to check."],"durationSeconds":5.135026899999997,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ba79a434-fa96-4866-9e1b-f80179e2f271","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"71c16390-9020-4f8a-9619-16a9257d0e85","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"70151134-3c76-4826-9770-fe0ea48e371f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"998498a1-a27e-413b-add6-ea4b12d88e02","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VCiXrvtaTKoPfQJ4jRhEv8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Bally The Shadow 1994 pinball manual pdf solenoid table ball launch\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Shadow (pinball)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Shadow_(pinball)\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow Pinball Manual - Bally - 1994-\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.de/itm/126990145325\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow\",\"url\":\"https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/The_Shadow\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/machine/shadow/details\"},{\"title\":\"(Topic ID: 93267)\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/shadow-manual-pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow\",\"url\":\"https://pinpedia.com/machine/The-Shadow\"},{\"title\":\"the shadow pinball machine\",\"url\":\"https://vintagearcade.net/shop/pinball-games/the-shadow-pinball-machine/\"},{\"title\":\"the shadow pinball tutorial\",\"url\":\"https://www.kineticist.com/post/the-shadow-pinball-tutorial\"},{\"title\":\"Shadow, The\",\"url\":\"https://www.arcade-museum.com/Pinball/shadow-the\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow [Model 50032]\",\"url\":\"https://www.arcade-history.com/game/5301/\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up a complete, downloadable PDF of the manual, and nothing specific about the solenoid table or ball launch circuit.\n\n- **Manual availability:** A Pinside forum thread asks for a complete manual PDF. Users there say the copies they found were missing many pages, and the thread is locked behind a free account. Does anyone have a complete PDF for The Shadow manual? All the ones I'm finding like on ipdb, are incomplete... missing pages 2-7 to 2-49.\n- **Ball launch:** The only launch-related detail is a revision note. Revision L-2 (December 6, 1994) enhanced ball shooter and ball save logic. The search results don't describe the launch solenoid or its wiring.\n- **Autofire plunger:** PinWiki says the manual calls out part A-2306-A. This is incorrect. Check the part number before ordering.\n- **Lower phurba ramp:** PinWiki also reports that fast shots to the lower phurba ramp diverted to the right sometimes get stuck because the switch wireform hangs the ball up.\n- **Game basics:** The game was made by Midway under the Bally label, with Midway WPC-Security, Model Number: 50032, and 4,247 units were built.\n\nFor the full manual, try the Pinside forum thread, the International Pinball Database, or the Pinside manual listings. For solenoid and launch troubleshooting, the PinWiki page and the WPC-specific notes it links to are the most useful starting points.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c275079b-24ee-42c1-a382-9b89c5538e7d","timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:11:36.608Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Bally The Shadow 1994 pinball manual pdf solenoid table ball launch","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Vtx3m7psKwjHwJHwGiqnXE","content":[{"title":"The Shadow (pinball)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Shadow_(pinball)"},{"title":"The Shadow Pinball Manual - Bally - 1994-","url":"https://www.ebay.de/itm/126990145325"},{"title":"The Shadow","url":"https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/The_Shadow"},{"title":"The Shadow","url":"https://pinside.com/pinball/machine/shadow/details"},{"title":"(Topic ID: 93267)","url":"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/shadow-manual-pdf"},{"title":"The Shadow","url":"https://pinpedia.com/machine/The-Shadow"},{"title":"the shadow pinball machine","url":"https://vintagearcade.net/shop/pinball-games/the-shadow-pinball-machine/"},{"title":"the shadow pinball tutorial","url":"https://www.kineticist.com/post/the-shadow-pinball-tutorial"},{"title":"Shadow, The","url":"https://www.arcade-museum.com/Pinball/shadow-the"},{"title":"The Shadow [Model 50032]","url":"https://www.arcade-history.com/game/5301/"}]},"The search didn't turn up a complete, downloadable PDF of the manual, and nothing specific about the solenoid table or ball launch circuit.\n\n- **Manual availability:** A Pinside forum thread asks for a complete manual PDF. Users there say the copies they found were missing many pages, and the thread is locked behind a free account. Does anyone have a complete PDF for The Shadow manual? All the ones I'm finding like on ipdb, are incomplete... missing pages 2-7 to 2-49.\n- **Ball launch:** The only launch-related detail is a revision note. Revision L-2 (December 6, 1994) enhanced ball shooter and ball save logic. The search results don't describe the launch solenoid or its wiring.\n- **Autofire plunger:** PinWiki says the manual calls out part A-2306-A. This is incorrect. Check the part number before ordering.\n- **Lower phurba ramp:** PinWiki also reports that fast shots to the lower phurba ramp diverted to the right sometimes get stuck because the switch wireform hangs the ball up.\n- **Game basics:** The game was made by Midway under the Bally label, with Midway WPC-Security, Model Number: 50032, and 4,247 units were built.\n\nFor the full manual, try the Pinside forum thread, the International Pinball Database, or the Pinside manual listings. For solenoid and launch troubleshooting, the PinWiki page and the WPC-specific notes it links to are the most useful starting points."],"durationSeconds":5.429790799999958,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ba79a434-fa96-4866-9e1b-f80179e2f271","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"70151134-3c76-4826-9770-fe0ea48e371f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","hash":"b4a20274b4ef2b3e363a244f6e87af05cf0cfa9555713752c6e8926a8cae4cec","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016gbEbxNmrx6SBQSwDrZRTN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"WPC power driver board A-12697 schematic fuse F103 solenoid 50V TIP36C TIP102\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Leon Borre Williams WPC and WPC-95 Driver Board Repair\",\"url\":\"https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/Leon_Borre_Williams_WPC_and_WPC-95_Driver_Board_Repair\"},{\"title\":\"Page 32 - WilliamsMidway WPC 91 Schematics 16-9289\",\"url\":\"https://planetarypinball.com/reference/partsmanuals/WMS_Schematic_WPC_16-9289/files/assets/seo/page32.html\"},{\"title\":\"WPC Power Driver Board - Replacement A-12697\",\"url\":\"https://www.planetarypinball.com/pinball-A-12697-TH\"},{\"title\":\"Power driver board – A-12697-x\",\"url\":\"https://www.pinball.co.uk/spares-accessories/power-driver-board-a-12697-x/\"},{\"title\":\"Power driver board – A-12697-x\",\"url\":\"https://www.pinball.co.uk/?p=35753\"},{\"title\":\"WPC89 Power Driver PCB Assy A-12697 (-1, -2, -3, -4)\",\"url\":\"https://www.planetarypinball.com/pinball-A-12697\"},{\"title\":\"WPC PDA12697X\",\"url\":\"https://www.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/WPC-PDA12697X\"},{\"title\":\"A 12697 1 3 4 WDB089 Bally Williams WPC89 WPC S Driver Board Pinball Machine  155239635245\",\"url\":\"https://napoleonexhibit.com/store/A-12697-1-3-4-WDB089-Bally-Williams-WPC89-WPC-S-Driver-Board-Pinball-Machine-_155239635245.html\"},{\"title\":\"Page 33 - Williams GREEN Parts Catalog 16-9932\",\"url\":\"https://www.planetarypinball.com/reference/partsmanuals/WMS_Parts_Green_16-9932/files/assets/seo/page33.html\"}]\n\nThe search turned up the board's general role and some background on the transistors, but nothing specific about fuse F103.\n\n- **Board function:** A Williams reference manual says the A-12697 power driver board handles the lamp, flipper, and solenoid circuits and supplies the +50V rail for solenoids, alongside +18V for lamps, +5V for logic, and +12V for switches. It contains no game-specific components, so it can be moved between games.\n- **Solenoid circuit troubleshooting:** A guide on the Pinwiki site describes tracing faulty high-current solenoid outputs through pre-driver, driver, and power transistor stages using the schematic and a test LED strip. It doesn't name F103 specifically.\n- **TIP102 and TIP36C:** A PinLED product page says the original design used TIP 102, 107, and 36C transistors, which become very hot in operation. That is the vendor's marketing claim, and its replacement uses MOSFETs instead.\n- **Fuses:** The PinLED page notes that its board includes LEDs to monitor the solenoid fuses and prints the fuse values on the layout. This suggests the fuse values are documented on the replacement board's silkscreen, not necessarily on the original schematic.\n- **Schematics:** The Williams parts catalog says schematics for these boards are in the operation manuals, not in the parts lists.\n\nI didn't find the schematic itself, the F103 fuse rating, or a confirmed TIP36C/TIP102 location on the A-12697. For those, the Williams WPC operation/service manual or the Pinwiki schematic images are the next places to check.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VCiXrvtaTKoPfQJ4jRhEv8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Bally The Shadow 1994 pinball manual pdf solenoid table ball launch\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Shadow (pinball)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Shadow_(pinball)\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow Pinball Manual - Bally - 1994-\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.de/itm/126990145325\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow\",\"url\":\"https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/The_Shadow\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/machine/shadow/details\"},{\"title\":\"(Topic ID: 93267)\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/shadow-manual-pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow\",\"url\":\"https://pinpedia.com/machine/The-Shadow\"},{\"title\":\"the shadow pinball machine\",\"url\":\"https://vintagearcade.net/shop/pinball-games/the-shadow-pinball-machine/\"},{\"title\":\"the shadow pinball tutorial\",\"url\":\"https://www.kineticist.com/post/the-shadow-pinball-tutorial\"},{\"title\":\"Shadow, The\",\"url\":\"https://www.arcade-museum.com/Pinball/shadow-the\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow [Model 50032]\",\"url\":\"https://www.arcade-history.com/game/5301/\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up a complete, downloadable PDF of the manual, and nothing specific about the solenoid table or ball launch circuit.\n\n- **Manual availability:** A Pinside forum thread asks for a complete manual PDF. Users there say the copies they found were missing many pages, and the thread is locked behind a free account. Does anyone have a complete PDF for The Shadow manual? All the ones I'm finding like on ipdb, are incomplete... missing pages 2-7 to 2-49.\n- **Ball launch:** The only launch-related detail is a revision note. Revision L-2 (December 6, 1994) enhanced ball shooter and ball save logic. The search results don't describe the launch solenoid or its wiring.\n- **Autofire plunger:** PinWiki says the manual calls out part A-2306-A. This is incorrect. Check the part number before ordering.\n- **Lower phurba ramp:** PinWiki also reports that fast shots to the lower phurba ramp diverted to the right sometimes get stuck because the switch wireform hangs the ball up.\n- **Game basics:** The game was made by Midway under the Bally label, with Midway WPC-Security, Model Number: 50032, and 4,247 units were built.\n\nFor the full manual, try the Pinside forum thread, the International Pinball Database, or the Pinside manual listings. For solenoid and launch troubleshooting, the PinWiki page and the WPC-specific notes it links to are the most useful starting points.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XByBBqzRVsCBsToADWuA8a","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"pinwiki WPC repair coil locked on at power up shorted transistor power driver board\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Terminator 2: Judgement Day\",\"url\":\"https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/Terminator_2:_Judgement_Day\"},{\"title\":\"Pinball Solenoid Stays Locked On\",\"url\":\"https://homepinballrepair.com/pinball-solenoid-stays-locked-on/\"},{\"title\":\"Coil & Lamp Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.pinball.co.uk/?p=20716\"},{\"title\":\"(Topic ID: 395093)\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/t2-board-issues\"},{\"title\":\"WPC Solenoid Troubleshooting\",\"url\":\"https://homepinballrepair.com/?p=5601\"},{\"title\":\"Coil testing\",\"url\":\"https://archive.maaca.org/s107351202.onlinehome.us/cgi-bin/Blah/Blah2c8c.html\"},{\"title\":\"Journalist Tool\",\"url\":\"https://jt.kineticist.com/items/55b1b637-d992-4738-b879-fcd56b25b494\"},{\"title\":\"(Topic ID: 12021)\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/jackbot-fusecoil-issues\"},{\"title\":\"(Topic ID: 64040)\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/collins-jackbot-issues-round-3\"}]\n\nThe search turned up several sources on coils that lock on at power-up, mostly from PinWiki and pinball forums.\n\n- **Missing diode tieback (Terminator 2):** The PinWiki page says a missing diode tieback wire can kill driver transistor Q20, and the coil then tends to lock on and overheat. The page suggests checking the J122 connector first, or adding a jumper wire from J122 pin 9 to J107 pin 2 as a more reliable fix. Without this \"diode tieback\", Q20 on the driver board WILL be damaged and the associated coil is likely to become locked on and melt. Another very reliable way to ensure that the diode tieback never loses connectivity, is to connect an additional wire, running from J122 pin 9 to J107 pin 2.\n\n- **Testing for a shorted transistor:** A MAACA post recommends measuring each coil's resistance before first power-up. If the resistance is higher than 2.5 ohms, the coil is good but the solenoid driver board transistor is shorted and will need to be replaced. The same post warns that if the solenoid driver board (SDB) transistor is repaired, and the game is powered on with a dead-shorted coil, this will blow the SDB's same transistor again, so check the coil first.\n\n- **Logic-probe and meter checks:** A homepinballrepair.com WPC guide suggests briefly grounding the transistor tab to see whether the coil fires. If the coil fires but the transistor still shows voltage across it, the transistor is shorted. That guide also notes If you have a shorted TIP, you likely have fried the pre-driver transistor 2N5401.\n\n- **Power driver board capacitors:** A Pinside forum thread on a WPC game recommends replacing the capacitors C4 and C2 on the power driver board, since C4 is well known for +5v problems. This is a separate suspect from the transistor, but it's worth checking on an older board.\n\n- **Power-up locking on:** A Pinball Rehab article describes a jet bumper that locks on every time the game powers up. It warns that if the game is not turned off immediately this problem can at best blow the solenoid fuse or at worst fry the coil or circuitry on the power supply board. Turn the game off right away if a coil locks on.\n\nI didn't find a page on PinWiki that matches your exact symptom, so these are the closest matches. The most common causes are a shorted driver transistor, a missing diode tieback, or a bad pre-driver transistor. Check each coil's resistance before powering the game on again.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}}
