e0fa78a","timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:11:50.843Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"6c66f757-a133-4b1f-9db9-90d73e0fa78a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"998498a1-a27e-413b-add6-ea4b12d88e02","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PfQUHy9Xtv8KbVwsuv8gtj","type":"tool_result","content":"The server returned HTTP 403 Forbidden.\n\nThe response body was not retrieved. If this URL requires authentication, use an authenticated tool (e.g. `gh` for GitHub, or an MCP-provided fetch tool) instead of WebFetch."}]},"uuid":"2482a276-719f-4d5f-bfdf-714c84afc3e4","timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:11:51.826Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":0,"code":403,"codeText":"Forbidden","result":"The server returned HTTP 403 Forbidden.\n\nThe response body was not retrieved. If this URL requires authentication, use an authenticated tool (e.g. `gh` for GitHub, or an MCP-provided fetch tool) instead of WebFetch.","durationMs":223,"url":"https://www.ipdb.org/machine.cgi?id=2528"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e5d5092c-8665-4389-8536-0339fce286bf","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6c66f757-a133-4b1f-9db9-90d73e0fa78a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"9f14d711-3f46-47e1-a2e2-991bfffefaef","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"998498a1-a27e-413b-add6-ea4b12d88e02","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J1j3yuijErndLxZ9kKVZmj","type":"tool_result","content":"The page doesn't contain a full solenoid/coil list, coil part numbers, power driver board notes, drop target info, fuse info, or schematic links. It is marked as a work in progress. Here is the technical content it does include:\n\n**Machine info**\n- Manufacturer: Bally. System: WPC-Security. Year: 1994. Model: 50032. Produced: 4,247.\n- Related pages: a playing tips and rule sheet (the page doesn't exist yet), a shop guide, and WPC Specific Issues.\n\n**Autofire / ball launch**\n- The autofire plunger issue is the only launch-related item. The page says the manual's part number is wrong: \"The manual calls out part A-2306-A. This is incorrect.\"\n- It recommends part A-17767 for more consistent autofiring.\n\n**Solenoids and wiring**\n- The manual's solenoid table has wiring errors: \"The solenoid table listing in the manual for The Shadow shows incorrect wiring connections.\"\n- A corrected table (image only, no text) was provided by Pinsider Zaza, along with other improvements.\n- Kicker coil wires in the mini playfield should be zip-tied neatly to prevent chafing as the kicker moves side to side.\n\n**Switches and diodes**\n- Lower Phurba microswitch: Fast shots diverted right can hang up on the switch wireform. The fix is a microswitch with a long wire actuator, bent so it activates later down the ramp.\n- Phurba diverter leaf switches: If a diode is bad or missing, closing either switch can close two switch-matrix columns. Replace or add the diode on the affected switch.\n\n**Mini playfield (Battlefield)**\n- Check the IDC connector on the opto board for damage.\n\n**Known software issue**\n- Some LH6 ROMs display \"Just Say NO to Drugs\" in French when adjusting volume. Version LX-5 doesn't have this bug.\n\n**Repair logs**\n- A Pinside guide covers the worn Sanctum magnet area on the playfield.\n\n**Not on the page:** drop targets, power driver board, fuses, connectors beyond the IDC note, and any manual or schematic links."}]},"uuid":"8657fca3-88a9-4b80-a2b9-a240eea891cf","timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:12:04.659Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":21321,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The page doesn't contain a full solenoid/coil list, coil part numbers, power driver board notes, drop target info, fuse info, or schematic links. It is marked as a work in progress. Here is the technical content it does include:\n\n**Machine info**\n- Manufacturer: Bally. System: WPC-Security. Year: 1994. Model: 50032. Produced: 4,247.\n- Related pages: a playing tips and rule sheet (the page doesn't exist yet), a shop guide, and WPC Specific Issues.\n\n**Autofire / ball launch**\n- The autofire plunger issue is the only launch-related item. The page says the manual's part number is wrong: \"The manual calls out part A-2306-A. This is incorrect.\"\n- It recommends part A-17767 for more consistent autofiring.\n\n**Solenoids and wiring**\n- The manual's solenoid table has wiring errors: \"The solenoid table listing in the manual for The Shadow shows incorrect wiring connections.\"\n- A corrected table (image only, no text) was provided by Pinsider Zaza, along with other improvements.\n- Kicker coil wires in the mini playfield should be zip-tied neatly to prevent chafing as the kicker moves side to side.\n\n**Switches and diodes**\n- Lower Phurba microswitch: Fast shots diverted right can hang up on the switch wireform. The fix is a microswitch with a long wire actuator, bent so it activates later down the ramp.\n- Phurba diverter leaf switches: If a diode is bad or missing, closing either switch can close two switch-matrix columns. Replace or add the diode on the affected switch.\n\n**Mini playfield (Battlefield)**\n- Check the IDC connector on the opto board for damage.\n\n**Known software issue**\n- Some LH6 ROMs display \"Just Say NO to Drugs\" in French when adjusting volume. Version LX-5 doesn't have this bug.\n\n**Repair logs**\n- A Pinside guide covers the worn Sanctum magnet area on the playfield.\n\n**Not on the page:** drop targets, power driver board, fuses, connectors beyond the IDC note, and any manual or schematic links.","durationMs":13057,"url":"https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/The_Shadow"},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e5d5092c-8665-4389-8536-0339fce286bf","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9f14d711-3f46-47e1-a2e2-991bfffefaef","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","hash":"f1c0ac811dddbbcd1d750c3ae62636cc55699065a34b27d154684908371cccaa","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PfQUHy9Xtv8KbVwsuv8gtj","type":"tool_result","content":"The server returned HTTP 403 Forbidden.\n\nThe response body was not retrieved. If this URL requires authentication, use an authenticated tool (e.g. `gh` for GitHub, or an MCP-provided fetch tool) instead of WebFetch."},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J1j3yuijErndLxZ9kKVZmj","type":"tool_result","content":"The page doesn't contain a full solenoid/coil list, coil part numbers, power driver board notes, drop target info, fuse info, or schematic links. It is marked as a work in progress. Here is the technical content it does include:\n\n**Machine info**\n- Manufacturer: Bally. System: WPC-Security. Year: 1994. Model: 50032. Produced: 4,247.\n- Related pages: a playing tips and rule sheet (the page doesn't exist yet), a shop guide, and WPC Specific Issues.\n\n**Autofire / ball launch**\n- The autofire plunger issue is the only launch-related item. The page says the manual's part number is wrong: \"The manual calls out part A-2306-A. This is incorrect.\"\n- It recommends part A-17767 for more consistent autofiring.\n\n**Solenoids and wiring**\n- The manual's solenoid table has wiring errors: \"The solenoid table listing in the manual for The Shadow shows incorrect wiring connections.\"\n- A corrected table (image only, no text) was provided by Pinsider Zaza, along with other improvements.\n- Kicker coil wires in the mini playfield should be zip-tied neatly to prevent chafing as the kicker moves side to side.\n\n**Switches and diodes**\n- Lower Phurba microswitch: Fast shots diverted right can hang up on the switch wireform. The fix is a microswitch with a long wire actuator, bent so it activates later down the ramp.\n- Phurba diverter leaf switches: If a diode is bad or missing, closing either switch can close two switch-matrix columns. Replace or add the diode on the affected switch.\n\n**Mini playfield (Battlefield)**\n- Check the IDC connector on the opto board for damage.\n\n**Known software issue**\n- Some LH6 ROMs display \"Just Say NO to Drugs\" in French when adjusting volume. Version LX-5 doesn't have this bug.\n\n**Repair logs**\n- A Pinside guide covers the worn Sanctum magnet area on the playfield.\n\n**Not on the page:** drop targets, power driver board, fuses, connectors beyond the IDC note, and any manual or schematic links."},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UGBkHL7H99C3FpigmrK1jM","type":"tool_result","content":"The page doesn't contain the detailed A-12697 content you asked for. It doesn't describe the solenoid driver topology by group (sol 1-8, 9-16, flashers, general purpose), the latch, the diode tieback, fuses F101-F116, blanking, or a locked-coil procedure. It also doesn't mention TIP36C, TIP107, 2N5401, or 2N4401. It is a bench-test and repair guide for WPC and WPC-95 driver boards, and its troubleshooting is organized by output connector (J-numbers), not by solenoid group.\n\nHere is the related material the page does provide:\n\n- **Board types:** It lists A12697-1, A12697-3, and A12697-4 for WPC, and 20028 for WPC-95. The main difference it notes is that some WPC boards lack a flipper enable relay, which sits at the top left of the board.\n- **Test points:** For WPC, it gives expected voltages at TP1 (12 V), TP2 (5 V), TP3 (12 V), TP6 (50 V), TP7 (20 V), and TP8 (18 V).\n- **Output groups and transistors:** Each connector section names the drivers and output transistors to follow. For example, the J130 group (\"High current solenoids\") runs from U5 through pre-drivers Q71-Q74 and Q59-Q62, drivers Q63-Q69 (odd numbers), and output transistors Q64-Q70 and Q76-Q82 (even numbers). The page's listings for some groups don't match cleanly, so check them against the schematic.\n- **Failure patterns:** For general purpose outputs, it says that when an output is missing, \"Mostly it will be the power outputs ( TIP102) that will go bad..\" It also notes that if the flipper enable relay never clicks, you should \"replace Q99.\"\n- **General illumination (J121, J106):** The page attributes stuck-on lamps to the TRIAC, with the drivers listed as Q17, Q9, Q13, Q15, Q11 and the TRIACs as Q18, Q10, Q14, Q16, Q12 for J121. For J106 it lists drivers Q6-Q8 and TRIACs Q13, Q4, Q5. It also names diodes D25, D26, D29, and D30 for the unswitched outputs.\n- **Lamp columns (J138, J123):** These need a voltmeter rather than the LED strip, because the polarity is reversed. The page names U9, U18, U19, and Q91-Q98 for J138, and U10, U11, and Q93-Q100 for J123.\n- **Test procedure:** A signal generator box drives the board through J113 (J102 on some boards), with a 5 V feed from a test point. Connect only J101 and J103 (or J127-J129 on WPC-95) first to check the power supplies, and confirm the control LEDs blink before testing outputs.\n\nFor the A-12697 solenoid driver details, you'll need the original schematic (the page links to \"WPC_power_drive_board.pdf\") or a dedicated A-12697 service document."}]}}
