,"attributionSkill":"superpowers:systematic-debugging","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"e9ae34bb-5d4a-47c4-a457-3a3de61bfe74","timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:12:21.866Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"3f893826-dea8-4ae9-8f0b-836fb01e13ae","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"998498a1-a27e-413b-add6-ea4b12d88e02","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JMp9HP3xkMCvZMWmSoZnnX","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"The Shadow\" Bally 50032 operations manual pdf download WPC schematics\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"BALLY THE SHADOW OPERATION MANUAL Pdf Download\",\"url\":\"https://www.manualslib.com/manual/4043266/Bally-The-Shadow.html\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow Pinball Machine (1994) by Bally Manufacturing Co.\",\"url\":\"https://www.kineticist.com/games/pinball/the-shadow\"},{\"title\":\"16-50032-101 - SHADOW (Bally) Manual - Marco Specialties Pinball Parts\",\"url\":\"https://www.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/16-50032-101\"},{\"title\":\"Bally The Shadow Manuals\",\"url\":\"https://www.manualslib.com/products/Bally-The-Shadow-14823060.html\"},{\"title\":\"Williams/Bally Game Manuals\",\"url\":\"https://www.planetarypinball.com/williams-bally-game-manuals\"},{\"title\":\"Internet Pinball Machine Database: Midway 'The Shadow'\",\"url\":\"https://www.ipdb.org/machine.cgi?id=2528\"},{\"title\":\"Page 132 - The Shadow (Bally)\",\"url\":\"https://www.planetarypinball.com/reference/gamemanuals/The_Shadow_Bly/files/assets/basic-html/page132.html\"},{\"title\":\"Shadow Manual PDF\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/shadow-manual-pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow Pinball Operations Manual\",\"url\":\"https://manualzz.com/doc/26192930/bally-the-shadow-manual\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow (pinball)\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Shadow_(pinball)\"}]\n\nThe search turned up several places to get the manual for Bally The Shadow (model 50032), but none of them is a verified complete, legal download.\n\n- **Full manual:** The November 1994 Operations Manual (part 16-50032-101) covers operations, testing, parts, and Reference Diagrams & Schematics. Manualslib has a copy, though its listing shows only 22 pages, so it may be partial.\n- **IPDB:** The Internet Pinball Database lists the Operations Manual (November 1994, includes schematics, missing pages 2-47, 3-9), and it also has a Parts List and a Repair Kit document.\n- **Kineticist:** This site offers an Operations Manual with Schematics (November 1994 Final) PDF with DIP settings and schematics, plus a Service Bulletin SB 81 on the mini-playfield.\n- **Pinside forum:** Users reported that several copies online are incomplete... missing pages 2-7 to 2-49, and one commenter said the IPDB copy worked for them.\n- **Marco Specialties:** This retailer sells a physical copy and mentions a free .PDF version.\n\nI did not find a WPC-specific schematics set separate from the manual. The schematics are in Section Three of the operations manual.\n\nBecause the manual is copyrighted, check whether the source is authorized before downloading. The IPDB and Pinside copies are the most consistently mentioned, but you should compare page counts against the roughly 183-page full manual listed by Planetary Pinball before relying on one.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c10936db-e9cd-40ba-ba51-658e9998c216","timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:12:28.222Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"\"The Shadow\" Bally 50032 operations manual pdf download WPC schematics","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01HKiNz3c9upJK4k2uoMyQL9","content":[{"title":"BALLY THE SHADOW OPERATION MANUAL Pdf Download","url":"https://www.manualslib.com/manual/4043266/Bally-The-Shadow.html"},{"title":"The Shadow Pinball Machine (1994) by Bally Manufacturing Co.","url":"https://www.kineticist.com/games/pinball/the-shadow"},{"title":"16-50032-101 - SHADOW (Bally) Manual - Marco Specialties Pinball Parts","url":"https://www.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/16-50032-101"},{"title":"Bally The Shadow Manuals","url":"https://www.manualslib.com/products/Bally-The-Shadow-14823060.html"},{"title":"Williams/Bally Game Manuals","url":"https://www.planetarypinball.com/williams-bally-game-manuals"},{"title":"Internet Pinball Machine Database: Midway 'The Shadow'","url":"https://www.ipdb.org/machine.cgi?id=2528"},{"title":"Page 132 - The Shadow (Bally)","url":"https://www.planetarypinball.com/reference/gamemanuals/The_Shadow_Bly/files/assets/basic-html/page132.html"},{"title":"Shadow Manual PDF","url":"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/shadow-manual-pdf"},{"title":"The Shadow Pinball Operations Manual","url":"https://manualzz.com/doc/26192930/bally-the-shadow-manual"},{"title":"The Shadow (pinball)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Shadow_(pinball)"}]},"The search turned up several places to get the manual for Bally The Shadow (model 50032), but none of them is a verified complete, legal download.\n\n- **Full manual:** The November 1994 Operations Manual (part 16-50032-101) covers operations, testing, parts, and Reference Diagrams & Schematics. Manualslib has a copy, though its listing shows only 22 pages, so it may be partial.\n- **IPDB:** The Internet Pinball Database lists the Operations Manual (November 1994, includes schematics, missing pages 2-47, 3-9), and it also has a Parts List and a Repair Kit document.\n- **Kineticist:** This site offers an Operations Manual with Schematics (November 1994 Final) PDF with DIP settings and schematics, plus a Service Bulletin SB 81 on the mini-playfield.\n- **Pinside forum:** Users reported that several copies online are incomplete... missing pages 2-7 to 2-49, and one commenter said the IPDB copy worked for them.\n- **Marco Specialties:** This retailer sells a physical copy and mentions a free .PDF version.\n\nI did not find a WPC-specific schematics set separate from the manual. The schematics are in Section Three of the operations manual.\n\nBecause the manual is copyrighted, check whether the source is authorized before downloading. The IPDB and Pinside copies are the most consistently mentioned, but you should compare page counts against the roughly 183-page full manual listed by Planetary Pinball before relying on one."],"durationSeconds":5.4980425000000395,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0004d454-c0dd-484c-b4da-b2d907b1b019","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3f893826-dea8-4ae9-8f0b-836fb01e13ae","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"parentUuid":"51c6d478-3b24-41f4-ae93-a0d3706940de","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"998498a1-a27e-413b-add6-ea4b12d88e02","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HtW9a39YTTY23JGiW7V39G","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"Shadow\" pinball solenoid table \"ball launch\" 50032 coil AE-23-800 OR \"auto launch\" OR \"autofire\" WPC\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Electric Or Magnetic Patents (Class 273/121A)\",\"url\":\"https://patents.justia.com/patents-by-us-classification/273/121A\"},{\"title\":\"US4557483A - Ball shooting apparatus for pinball game machine - Google Patents\",\"url\":\"https://patents.google.com/patent/US4557483A/enExample\"},{\"title\":\"data.epo.org\",\"url\":\"https://data.epo.org/publication-server/rest/v1.2/patents/EP0294923NWA2/document.html\"},{\"title\":\"JPS6037370U - 遊戯機の球発射装置 - Google Patents\",\"url\":\"https://patents.google.com/patent/JPS6037370U/enExample\"},{\"title\":\"Ball shooting apparatus for pinball game machine\",\"url\":\"https://patents.justia.com/patent/4557483\"},{\"title\":\"Plunger, Mechanically Or Electrically Driven Patents (Class 273/129S)\",\"url\":\"https://patents.justia.com/patents-by-us-classification/273/129S\"},{\"title\":\"US4790536A - Parallel coil pin ball flipper solenoid - Google Patents\",\"url\":\"https://patents.google.com/patent/US4790536\"},{\"title\":\"US5048832A - Double ball launcher for rolling ball game - Google Patents\",\"url\":\"https://patents.google.com/patent/US5048832A/en\"},{\"title\":\"Double ball launcher for rolling ball game\",\"url\":\"https://patents.justia.com/patent/5048832\"}]\n\nThe search didn't turn up anything specific to the Shadow table, the 50032 coil, AE-23-800, or WPC auto-launch/autofire. Every result was a patent or patent listing about pinball solenoids in general, so none of them can confirm the part numbers or the hardware behavior you asked about.\n\nThe general material that did come back:\n\n- **Launch solenoids in general:** One patent describes a solenoid that strikes the ball at a launch position and shoots it onto the playfield. A solenoid 8 is provided in order to strike the ball 2 at the launching position 1 and to shoot it onto the playing field 5.\n- **Automatic launch as a feature:** A Williams patent describes a launcher that fires balls at times set by the game's microprocessor, and it notes that pinball games have been provided in which an automatic launcher system is provided, for example, the Centaur brand pinball game. It also says the launch can be triggered by in-game events, such as a target being hit. The electrical means may be actuated by events during the game, for example when a certain target on the playfield is struck, or the like.\n- **Timed or randomized firing:** The same patent says the solenoid can fire after a set delay from an event, or at random once play starts. A timer may be actuated by such an event to actuate solenoid 32 after a predetermined time beginning with the event.\n\nFor the specific hardware, I'd check Shadow service manuals or schematics (Williams/Bally, 1995), WPC-95 technical documentation, and parts suppliers that list coil numbers. Those are more likely to confirm whether 50032 and AE-23-800 are the right part numbers for this table's launch circuit. I can run a narrower search on those if you want.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"193af06c-9756-41dd-9a66-89804b627626","timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:12:28.316Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"\"Shadow\" pinball solenoid table \"ball launch\" 50032 coil AE-23-800 OR \"auto launch\" OR \"autofire\" WPC","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01JuMKtUqnGoQSpj3gkSUR7Z","content":[{"title":"Electric Or Magnetic Patents (Class 273/121A)","url":"https://patents.justia.com/patents-by-us-classification/273/121A"},{"title":"US4557483A - Ball shooting apparatus for pinball game machine - Google Patents","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US4557483A/enExample"},{"title":"data.epo.org","url":"https://data.epo.org/publication-server/rest/v1.2/patents/EP0294923NWA2/document.html"},{"title":"JPS6037370U - 遊戯機の球発射装置 - Google Patents","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/JPS6037370U/enExample"},{"title":"Ball shooting apparatus for pinball game machine","url":"https://patents.justia.com/patent/4557483"},{"title":"Plunger, Mechanically Or Electrically Driven Patents (Class 273/129S)","url":"https://patents.justia.com/patents-by-us-classification/273/129S"},{"title":"US4790536A - Parallel coil pin ball flipper solenoid - Google Patents","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US4790536"},{"title":"US5048832A - Double ball launcher for rolling ball game - Google Patents","url":"https://patents.google.com/patent/US5048832A/en"},{"title":"Double ball launcher for rolling ball game","url":"https://patents.justia.com/patent/5048832"}]},"The search didn't turn up anything specific to the Shadow table, the 50032 coil, AE-23-800, or WPC auto-launch/autofire. Every result was a patent or patent listing about pinball solenoids in general, so none of them can confirm the part numbers or the hardware behavior you asked about.\n\nThe general material that did come back:\n\n- **Launch solenoids in general:** One patent describes a solenoid that strikes the ball at a launch position and shoots it onto the playfield. A solenoid 8 is provided in order to strike the ball 2 at the launching position 1 and to shoot it onto the playing field 5.\n- **Automatic launch as a feature:** A Williams patent describes a launcher that fires balls at times set by the game's microprocessor, and it notes that pinball games have been provided in which an automatic launcher system is provided, for example, the Centaur brand pinball game. It also says the launch can be triggered by in-game events, such as a target being hit. The electrical means may be actuated by events during the game, for example when a certain target on the playfield is struck, or the like.\n- **Timed or randomized firing:** The same patent says the solenoid can fire after a set delay from an event, or at random once play starts. A timer may be actuated by such an event to actuate solenoid 32 after a predetermined time beginning with the event.\n\nFor the specific hardware, I'd check Shadow service manuals or schematics (Williams/Bally, 1995), WPC-95 technical documentation, and parts suppliers that list coil numbers. Those are more likely to confirm whether 50032 and AE-23-800 are the right part numbers for this table's launch circuit. I can run a narrower search on those if you want."],"durationSeconds":5.588009699999995,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0004d454-c0dd-484c-b4da-b2d907b1b019","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"51c6d478-3b24-41f4-ae93-a0d3706940de","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
