Ployfield or \n ! \n Backbox Coil \n 4700 \n 680 \n xf-+------, \n Brown-XXX \n LS374 \n 2.7KO \n FI12 \n J107 \n F104 \n + \n Red-Block \n : \n 1001'1 \n i \n s \n 'W \n I:: \n POWER \n t. \n ~ \n J \n The microprocessor toggles the output of the 74LS374. \n When point \"A\" is low, point \"8\" the collector of the 2N5401 transistor is \n driven high. A high at point \"8\" turns On the TIP102 transistor, and causes point \n \"CO \n to drop low. When point \n \"C\" \n is low the coil is \n grounded through the transistor and the coil turns On. The coil shuts Off when point \"A\" toggles high. \n 3-8 \n Planetary Pinball Supply, Inc","is_error":false}]}}
