{"parentUuid":"b8191e15-1c8f-44f1-8b3d-a51e8de84b6e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"998498a1-a27e-413b-add6-ea4b12d88e02","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DqjZravDPBwJoeFGNJYUkz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Shadow pinball solenoid table manual incorrect wiring corrected table Zaza pinside\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Shadow\",\"url\":\"https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/The_Shadow\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow pinball machine repair guide\",\"url\":\"https://www.pinball.co.uk/?p=20721\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow pinball machine repair guide\",\"url\":\"https://www.pinball.co.uk/pinball-problems/the-shadow-pinball-machine-repair-guide/\"},{\"title\":\"by date\",\"url\":\"https://planetarypinball.com/mm5/Williams/tech/by_date.html\"},{\"title\":\"(Topic ID: 127339)\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/the-shadow-gi-help\"},{\"title\":\"The Correctifier\",\"url\":\"https://www.robmiles.com/journal/2012/8/18/the-correctifier.html\"},{\"title\":\"Service Bulletin: SB 49\",\"url\":\"https://www.planetarypinball.com/mm5/Williams/tech/sb49.html\"},{\"title\":\"(Topic ID: 32670)\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/the-shadow-wall-problem\"},{\"title\":\"(Topic ID: 197121)\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/shadow-up-down-weird-problem\"}]\n\nThe main hit is the PinWiki page for The Shadow, which says the manual's solenoid table is wrong and that a corrected version exists. That corrected table is an image, so the search results don't include the actual wiring fixes.\n\n- **The corrected table:** PinWiki says the table was shared with permission from Pinsider Sascha Voskuil, who goes by Zaza. It also notes that the corrected version includes a few other improvements. The corrected Shadow solenoid table was provided with permission by Pinsider Sascha Voskuil aka Zaza. The solenoid table listing in the manual for The Shadow shows incorrect wiring connections. The corrected table, along with a few other improvements to the table, is shown on the left.\n- **Related bulletin:** The search also returned a 1993 WMS service bulletin for Creature from the Black Lagoon, not The Shadow. It shows the same kind of problem, where the manual's solenoid table had a wrong connector reference that the bulletin corrected. It is useful only as a parallel.\n- **Pinside threads:** Two Pinside threads touch on Shadow wiring. One describes a wall-target solenoid that works backwards, and a commenter suggests the solenoid wires may be swapped. The other covers a GI connector whose manual wire color doesn't match the machine. Neither mentions the Zaza table directly.\n\nTo get the actual corrected wiring, open the PinWiki page and look at its image, or search Pinside for Zaza's Shadow solenoid table thread.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8fa34964-f1fb-42da-b660-4bf90d8a74c6","timestamp":"2026-10-25T10:24:49.622Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Shadow pinball solenoid table manual incorrect wiring corrected table Zaza pinside","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01MCiMixmeUdTgKpoqUFduHa","content":[{"title":"The Shadow","url":"https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/The_Shadow"},{"title":"The Shadow pinball machine repair guide","url":"https://www.pinball.co.uk/?p=20721"},{"title":"The Shadow pinball machine repair guide","url":"https://www.pinball.co.uk/pinball-problems/the-shadow-pinball-machine-repair-guide/"},{"title":"by date","url":"https://planetarypinball.com/mm5/Williams/tech/by_date.html"},{"title":"(Topic ID: 127339)","url":"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/the-shadow-gi-help"},{"title":"The Correctifier","url":"https://www.robmiles.com/journal/2012/8/18/the-correctifier.html"},{"title":"Service Bulletin: SB 49","url":"https://www.planetarypinball.com/mm5/Williams/tech/sb49.html"},{"title":"(Topic ID: 32670)","url":"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/the-shadow-wall-problem"},{"title":"(Topic ID: 197121)","url":"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/shadow-up-down-weird-problem"}]},"The main hit is the PinWiki page for The Shadow, which says the manual's solenoid table is wrong and that a corrected version exists. That corrected table is an image, so the search results don't include the actual wiring fixes.\n\n- **The corrected table:** PinWiki says the table was shared with permission from Pinsider Sascha Voskuil, who goes by Zaza. It also notes that the corrected version includes a few other improvements. The corrected Shadow solenoid table was provided with permission by Pinsider Sascha Voskuil aka Zaza. The solenoid table listing in the manual for The Shadow shows incorrect wiring connections. The corrected table, along with a few other improvements to the table, is shown on the left.\n- **Related bulletin:** The search also returned a 1993 WMS service bulletin for Creature from the Black Lagoon, not The Shadow. It shows the same kind of problem, where the manual's solenoid table had a wrong connector reference that the bulletin corrected. It is useful only as a parallel.\n- **Pinside threads:** Two Pinside threads touch on Shadow wiring. One describes a wall-target solenoid that works backwards, and a commenter suggests the solenoid wires may be swapped. The other covers a GI connector whose manual wire color doesn't match the machine. Neither mentions the Zaza table directly.\n\nTo get the actual corrected wiring, open the PinWiki page and look at its image, or search Pinside for Zaza's Shadow solenoid table thread."],"durationSeconds":4.868484399999957,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c1765a31-40c3-49ad-8fb8-15dbdde3e2a8","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","root":null,"branch":null,"default_branch":null,"status":null,"visibility":{"origin":null,"push_remote":null,"remotes":[],"visibility_cache":[]},"error":"not_a_repo"},"live_cwd":"/c/sources/the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","platform":"windows"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b8191e15-1c8f-44f1-8b3d-a51e8de84b6e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"session_id":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","hash":"dad7d89f0349828df472fc8568539a436437136878bcb95fc51ee544e2d3239e","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DqjZravDPBwJoeFGNJYUkz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Shadow pinball solenoid table manual incorrect wiring corrected table Zaza pinside\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"The Shadow\",\"url\":\"https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/The_Shadow\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow pinball machine repair guide\",\"url\":\"https://www.pinball.co.uk/?p=20721\"},{\"title\":\"The Shadow pinball machine repair guide\",\"url\":\"https://www.pinball.co.uk/pinball-problems/the-shadow-pinball-machine-repair-guide/\"},{\"title\":\"by date\",\"url\":\"https://planetarypinball.com/mm5/Williams/tech/by_date.html\"},{\"title\":\"(Topic ID: 127339)\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/the-shadow-gi-help\"},{\"title\":\"The Correctifier\",\"url\":\"https://www.robmiles.com/journal/2012/8/18/the-correctifier.html\"},{\"title\":\"Service Bulletin: SB 49\",\"url\":\"https://www.planetarypinball.com/mm5/Williams/tech/sb49.html\"},{\"title\":\"(Topic ID: 32670)\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/the-shadow-wall-problem\"},{\"title\":\"(Topic ID: 197121)\",\"url\":\"https://pinside.com/pinball/forum/topic/shadow-up-down-weird-problem\"}]\n\nThe main hit is the PinWiki page for The Shadow, which says the manual's solenoid table is wrong and that a corrected version exists. That corrected table is an image, so the search results don't include the actual wiring fixes.\n\n- **The corrected table:** PinWiki says the table was shared with permission from Pinsider Sascha Voskuil, who goes by Zaza. It also notes that the corrected version includes a few other improvements. The corrected Shadow solenoid table was provided with permission by Pinsider Sascha Voskuil aka Zaza. The solenoid table listing in the manual for The Shadow shows incorrect wiring connections. The corrected table, along with a few other improvements to the table, is shown on the left.\n- **Related bulletin:** The search also returned a 1993 WMS service bulletin for Creature from the Black Lagoon, not The Shadow. It shows the same kind of problem, where the manual's solenoid table had a wrong connector reference that the bulletin corrected. It is useful only as a parallel.\n- **Pinside threads:** Two Pinside threads touch on Shadow wiring. One describes a wall-target solenoid that works backwards, and a commenter suggests the solenoid wires may be swapped. The other covers a GI connector whose manual wire color doesn't match the machine. Neither mentions the Zaza table directly.\n\nTo get the actual corrected wiring, open the PinWiki page and look at its image, or search Pinside for Zaza's Shadow solenoid table thread.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PeUnZL6HCaE6f1k7nmZVHa","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"AE-23-800 coil resistance ohms Williams Bally chart AE-25-1000 AE-26-1200 AE-26-1500\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Coil Substitutions and Equivalents\",\"url\":\"https://www.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts-blog/coil-subs/\"},{\"title\":\"Flat Rate Shipping: $9.99+\",\"url\":\"https://www.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/090-5001-00\"},{\"title\":\"COIL - SLINGSHOT MULTIMORPHIC 23-800\",\"url\":\"https://www.marcospecialties.com:443/pinball-parts/COIL-1023-0800\"},{\"title\":\"coil solenoid data east sega stern 090 5001 00\",\"url\":\"https://www.pinballshop.nl/electronics-parts/coils-and-sleeve/coil-solenoid-data-east-sega-stern-090-5001-00/\"},{\"title\":\"COIL 3023 0600\",\"url\":\"https://www.marcospecialties.com:443/pinball-parts/COIL-3023-0600\"},{\"title\":\"090 5001 0T\",\"url\":\"https://test.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/090-5001-0T\"},{\"title\":\"test.marcospecialties.com\",\"url\":\"https://test.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/090-5001-00\"},{\"title\":\"www.ebay.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.ebay.com/p/2242068103\"},{\"title\":\"Williams/Bally Coil AE27-1200 without Diode (NOTE: sleeves not usually included - and actual coil pi\",\"url\":\"https://www.planetarypinball.com/pinball-27-1200\"},{\"title\":\"coil flipper blue fl 11629\",\"url\":\"https://www.pinballshop.nl/electronics-parts/coils-and-sleeve/coil-flipper-blue-fl-11629/\"}]\n\nI found a resistance figure for the AE-23-800 family, but nothing for AE-25-1000, AE-26-1200, or AE-26-1500.\n\n- **AE-23-800:** A Marco Specialties listing gives Wire Gauge: 23, Number of turns: 800, Resistance in ohms: 3.6 for a Data East/Sega/Stern coil (090-5001-00). That listing says it was Replaced by AE-23-800-01 as an equivalent substitute, so 3.6 ohms is the best available figure for AE-23-800-01, though it comes from a related part rather than a Williams/Bally spec sheet.\n- **Related coil, not the same part:** Marco's Multimorphic slingshot coil, COIL-1023-0800, is listed at Resistance in ohms: 3.5 with the same 23 gauge and 800 turns.\n- **AE-26-1200, AE-26-1500, AE-25-1000:** Retailer listings confirm these coils exist, such as an eBay listing for Williams Bally Pinball Machine Solenoid Coil - Ae-26-1500, but the results show no resistance values for them. A Planetary Pinball listing for AE27-1200 also omits resistance.\n\nFor verified values on the AE-25 and AE-26 coils, check a Williams/Bally service manual or a multimeter reading on a known-good coil.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]}}
