{"parentUuid":"82a2e9ca-2209-43fa-bd84-b0a332efc76c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"998498a1-a27e-413b-add6-ea4b12d88e02","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, PowerShell, Read, Skill, ToolSearch, WebFetch, WebSearch, Write</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (French-speaking; all replies must be in French with correct accents) pasted one detailed request: act as an electronics expert in Bally/Williams pinballs and their Power Driver boards to diagnose and repair their **Bally The Shadow (1994)**. Requirements, in substance:\n   - Rigorous, independent diagnosis based on the schematics and real measurements. \"**Ne considère jamais mes hypothèses comme des diagnostics confirmés. N'hésite pas à me contredire si les preuves l'exigent.**\"\n   - Find the exact manual and the Power Driver and wiring schematics; verify part references and connections; \"N'invente pas d'informations manquantes. Si nécessaire, demande-moi une photo, un document ou une mesure.\"\n   - Known history (uncertain memories): an initial short, possibly in the upper playfield near the mini-playfield or a drop target; F103 seemed to blow; a transistor burned; a Power Driver diode burned (replaced, and an identified short was fixed); afterwards several transistors seemed to overheat, with \"points lumineux sur la carte, vers le bas à droite\"; several components replaced without certainty that all damage was repaired.\n   - Current symptom: from power-on, the auto Ball Launch coil (start of the shooter lane) stays energized; the plunger is held by the magnet. Cause unknown (board, wiring or other).\n   - **Priority goal: \"Avant de reconnecter une Power Driver réparée, je veux vérifier méthodiquement que le câblage et les composants du flipper ne présentent pas de défaut susceptible de la détruire à nouveau.\"** Earlier connector measurements were not organized enough to count as validation.\n   - Method: separate confirmed observations, uncertain memories and hypotheses; favour no cause without technical justification; identify the most discriminating tests; \"Guide-moi une seule manipulation ou mesure à la fois\"; say where, how and how to interpret each measurement; prefer off-power checks and account for charged capacitors; \"**Ne propose aucune remise sous tension avant d'avoir évalué les risques et les contrôles nécessaires.**\"; explain enough electronics to be understood; concise but rigorous, no repetition.\n   - Maintain `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (situation summary, known faults and repairs, measurements and results, confirmed/rejected/pending hypotheses, checks before reconnection, next step), keep useful history without inventing results, update it after significant steps, make it reusable in a new conversation.\n   - Start: study the docs and symptoms without assuming a cause, build a strategy that prioritizes protecting the Power Driver, briefly present the initial reasoning, guide the first safe and relevant check, then **wait for the user's result**.\n   - Global CLAUDE.md constraints (verbatim intent): never add a `Co-Authored-By: Claude ...` trailer to commits; never add a Claude attribution footer (e.g. \"🤖 Generated with [Claude Code]\") to PR descriptions. These override the harness attribution reminders. (No git repo here; not currently relevant.)\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - The Shadow: Bally/Midway 1994, model 50032, WPC-S (Security). Boards: CPU Security, Power Driver (PD) A-12697-x (manual describes the -3), Fliptronic II, DCS sound, DMD controller.\n   - Sol 01 drive chain (A-12697-1 schematic, sheet 3): CPU → J113 → U5 74LS374 (OC/OE pin 1 tied to BLANKING, J113-31) → R135 470Ω → Q71 2N5401 (R134 4.7k pull-up to VCC) → R124 68Ω → Q81 TIP102 (R123 2.7k) → Q82 TIP36C (R125 220Ω B-E; collector to ground; emitter = drive line J130-1). D32 1N4004 on-board flyback from J130-1 to the 50V bus.\n   - Power path: J102 → F112 (7A SB) → BR3 → 50VDC (C8 100µF, R260 10k bleeder, TP6) → F105 (3A SB) → J107-2 Red-Brown → coil AE-23-800 → Violet-Brown → J130-1.\n   - Blanking: at power-up (CPU LED D19 on) the latch outputs are tri-stated, so a coil energized \"dès l'allumage\" points to a short downstream of U5 (Q82/Q81/Q71/solder bridge) or to wiring, not logic. CPU LEDs: at turn-on D19 and D21 on, D20 off; in normal operation D19 off, D20 flashing, D21 on.\n   - Fuse map (manual p.1-52): F101/F102 +50V general (left/right flipper) 3A SB; **F103 Sol #25–#28 = \"continuous duty\" 50V → J107-1 Red-Orange (feeds Sol 24 Mini Drop Bank, Sol 25 Single Drop Up, tieback)**; F104 Sol 9–16 (J107-3 Red-Black); **F105 Sol 1–8 (J107-2 Red-Brown)**; F106–F110 GI 5A SB; F111 flasher secondary 5A SB (BR4, 20V); F112 solenoid secondary 7A SB; F113 +5V 5A SB; F114 +18V lamps 8A 32V; F115 +12V switch 3/4A (FB on p.1-52, SB in parts list); F116 +12V secondary 3A SB; Fliptronic F901–F904 3A SB.\n   - Tieback: on-board diodes D9/D10/D12/D11 (Q28/Q30/Q34/Q32, J126 group) and D8/D7/D6/D5 (Q26/Q24/Q22/Q20, J122 group) have common cathodes out on J126-11 and J122-5, which the harness must tie to the Red-Orange 50V. Without it, the Sol 24 (Q32) and Sol 25 (Q26) TIP102s are unprotected.\n   - Unproven history hypothesis H-hist: Red-Orange shorted to ground → F103 blows and 20V flasher current is forced through the tieback diodes (one burns). Consistent with E1/E2/E4, does not explain Sol 01.\n   - AE-23-800 ≈ 3.5 Ω (vendor value for 23 AWG/800 turns, indicative); compare with Sol 07 Knocker and Sol 08 Wall Target Up (same coil). A locked-on coil draws roughly 14A, far above F105's 3A SB rating, so F105 should blow quickly; a long hold without it blowing is suspect (wrong fuse? transistor partly conducting?).\n   - PD LEDs: LED1 +12V switch, LED2/LED3 line sensor (LED3 normally off), LED4 +5V, LED5 +20V, LED6 +18V, LED7 +12V power; none sits in the lower-right area. Test points TP1 +12V, TP2 +5V, TP3 +12V, TP5 ground, TP6 +50V, TP7 +20V, TP8 +18V. Big caps C5, C6, C7, C11, C30 are 15,000µF 25V.\n   - Lower right of the board as mounted = J130 area (Q63–Q82, Sol 1–8) and lamp matrix (J133–J138, Q83–Q98).\n   - PinWiki: the manual's solenoid table has wiring errors (corrected table by \"Zaza\", image only), so always confirm by wire color and continuity. Mini Kicker (Sol 15, A-19070 coil/slide assembly on a motorized slide) wires can chafe and should be zip-tied. Autofire plunger part A-2306-A in the manual is wrong; A-17767 is recommended.\n   - The superpowers:systematic-debugging skill was invoked (root cause before fixes, one hypothesis and one test at a time).\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md** (CREATED): the main deliverable. Sections:\n     - §0 work rules, with tags [MESURÉ]/[OBSERVÉ]/[SOUVENIR]/[HYPOTHÈSE]/[DOC].\n     - §1 situation summary (PD state \"à confirmer\").\n     - §2 history table E1–E6 with technical comments.\n     - §3 reference data: Sol 01 chain diagram, fuse table, full solenoid table (Sol 01–28, 35, 36 with supply, fuse, transistor, PD pin, wire color, coil), tieback, LEDs, test points, capacitors.\n     - §4 observation/measurement table: O1 = symptom; M1 pending.\n     - §5 hypotheses for the symptom: H1 Q82 shorted, H2 Q81/Q71/solder bridge, H3 Violet-Brown to ground (test M1), H4 U5/blanking (weak), H5 mechanical (weak). Risks R1–R8: shorted coils, reversed/shorted diodes, drive-to-50V shorts, 50V cross-shorts (especially at the mini-playfield), missing tieback, wrong fuses, residual PD damage, collateral damage on CPU, opto boards, motor board A-16120 and Fliptronic.\n     - §6 H-hist.\n     - §7 checklist: Phase 0 safety and fuse inventory; A Sol 01 circuit; B all coil outputs plus tieback continuity J122-5 ↔ J126-11 ↔ J107-1 and Fliptronic Sol 35/36; C cross-shorts between voltage domains plus harness inspection; D bench checks of the PD (Q82, Q81, Q71, D32, D5–D12, D17–D32, BR3, C8/R260, solder bridges, glowing-points area); E progressive power-up protocol, to be defined.\n     - §8 next step M1 with interpretation.\n     - §9 open questions.\n     - §10 sources and local docs.\n   - **C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\docs\\** (CREATED, 5.3 MB), copies of reference material:\n     - `manuel-the-shadow/`: page-de-garde_tableau-solenoides.png, 1-51_LED.jpg, 1-52_fusibles.png, 1-55/1-56 mini-playfield, 2-8_PD_liste-pieces.png, 2-9_PD_implantation.jpg, 2-29_coil-slide-motor.jpg, 2-42_tableau-solenoides.jpg, 3-6_cablage-solenoides.jpg, 3-7_cablage-flashers.jpg, 3-8_circuits-HP-LP.jpg, fp162–fp164 carte-moteur-DC, 3-27/3-28/3-29 PD connecteurs.\n     - `schema-power-driver/`: schema_A-12697-1_16-9057.pdf plus zoomed crops (f3_etage-HP_Q71-Q82_sol01-04.png, f3_U5_74LS374_sol01-08.png, f3_J113_blanking.png, f3_J126_Q28-Q42_tieback-D9-D12.png, f3_J122_Q20-Q32_tieback-D5-D8.png, f1_distribution-50V_F101-F105.png, f1_BR3_F112_C8_R260.png).\n     - `theorie-wpc/`: 3-11 HP/LP, 3-12 flashers/GP tieback, 4-5 solenoid troubleshooting, 4-7 power troubleshooting.\n   - **Memory**: C:\\Users\\vladi\\.claude\\projects\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\memory\\shadow-diagnostic-method.md (feedback memory: one measurement per message, off-power first, no power-on before the checklist, never treat the user's recollections as confirmed, answer in French, read and update the journal and docs/) and MEMORY.md (index line).\n   - Scratchpad helper: scratchpad\\scripts\\crop.py (PyMuPDF crop/zoom of PDF regions; run with `python -E -P` because `-I` hid the user-site fitz module).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - IPDB returned 403 (WebFetch and Invoke-WebRequest); kineticist returned 429; pinball.co.uk returned 403. Fixed by using the Planetary Pinball flipbook instead.\n   - Flipbook basic-html page images were only background layers. Fixed by finding the mobile zoom images at `files/assets/mobile/pageNNNN_i2.png|jpg` (found via properties.xml and book.js).\n   - The WPC 16-9289 flipbook has no schematic fold-outs. Fixed by downloading the PinWiki PDF (`/wiki/images/5/5b/WPC_power_drive_board.pdf`).\n   - `python -I` raised ModuleNotFoundError for fitz. Fixed with `python -E -P`, keeping the script outside the downloads directory.\n   - No user feedback on errors so far.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Documentation research is done and key facts were cross-checked between the manual's table, connector lists, wiring diagram and the schematic. Sol 01 = Q82, J130-1 Violet-Brown, consistent in three places.\n   - The remembered F103 history is linked by documentation to the Red-Orange branch (Sol 24 on the mini-playfield, Sol 25), a different circuit from Sol 01 (F105). Two separate faults or a common cause both remain possible.\n   - Strategy chosen: wiring checks of the Sol 01 network first (the only symptom explanation outside the board), then all coils, cross-shorts, fuses, bench checks of the PD, and finally a progressive power-up.\n   - First measurement designed (M1). Its interpretation thresholds are in §6 and §9 below.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Only one user message: the pasted request \"# Diagnostic et réparation — Bally The Shadow (1994)\", content as in section 1. Its sections were: Ton rôle; Documentation; Historique connu; Symptôme actuel; Objectif prioritaire; Méthode de travail; Journal de diagnostic; Pour commencer (\"Présente brièvement ton raisonnement initial, puis guide-moi vers la première vérification sûre et pertinente. Attends mon résultat avant de continuer.\"). The user also ran `/effort max` locally. No other user messages.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Send the initial response (not yet sent; tool work was just finished) in French:\n     - brief initial reasoning: verified doc facts, symptom interpretation via blanking, the F103/Red-Orange link with the history, strategy phases;\n     - the first step: safety prerequisites plus measurement M1;\n     - the open questions;\n     - mention that the journal and docs/ were created;\n     - a \"Sources:\" list with markdown links (required by WebSearch).\n   - Then wait for the user's M1 result, update the journal (§4 table, hypothesis statuses, next step), and continue one measurement at a time following the §7 checklist.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   All research, docs copying, journal creation and memory writing are done. What remains is writing the user-facing answer. Planned content:\n   - **What the docs say**:\n     - Sol 01 Ball Launch: High Power, Q82 TIP36C, J130-1 Violet-Brown, coil AE-23-800, supply J107-2 Red-Brown via F105 3A SB.\n     - F103 = Red-Orange 50V for Sol 24 Mini Drop Bank (mini-playfield) and Sol 25 Single Drop Up plus the tieback. Consistent with the remembered short location, but a different circuit.\n     - Blanking keeps the outputs off at power-up.\n     - PinWiki warns that the manual's solenoid table has errors and that the Mini Kicker wires chafe.\n   - **Symptom reading**: the coil is on whenever the Violet-Brown wire reaches ground, either through Q82/Q81/Q71/a solder bridge or through the wiring. Logic is less likely if the coil is on immediately at power-on. A locked coil (~14A) should blow F105 quickly.\n   - **Simple ASCII chain** of the circuit.\n   - **Strategy phases** 0/A/B/C/D/E.\n   - **Step 1 prerequisites**:\n     - unplug the mains cord (the switch is not enough) and wait at least 5 minutes;\n     - disconnect all PD connectors if not already done, photographing them first;\n     - if the PD is still mounted, wait until its LEDs are off;\n     - do not touch the DMD controller (+62V, −113/−125V).\n   - **Mesure 1**:\n     - Meter on V DC, red probe on the Violet-Brown contact of the J130 harness connector (pin 1), black probe on J116-3 (Black ground, harness side; J118-3 as an alternative). Expect about 0 V; stop and report if above 1 V.\n     - Then ohms: first short the probes together and note the lead resistance; (a) J130-1 ↔ J116-3; (b) J130-1 ↔ earth (earth contact of the mains plug, or bare metal of the cabinet such as the coin-door frame or ground braid).\n     - Probe gently into the female contact without spreading it.\n   - **Interpretation**:\n     - OL on both: the Sol 1–8 network is isolated from ground, so the board output stage becomes the main suspect (to confirm with the coil resistance, since an open coil would hide the rest of the network);\n     - ≈0 Ω: Violet-Brown wire or coil lug grounded;\n     - ≈3–4 Ω (one coil): Red-Brown 50V bus grounded;\n     - higher, the sum of two coils: another Sol 2–8 drive wire grounded;\n     - intermediate value: abnormal link to investigate.\n   - **Questions**:\n     - Is the PD removed? Which parts were replaced (designators)?\n     - At the last power-on: how long was the coil held, did F105 blow, did the game boot normally (display, sounds, D20 flashing)?\n     - Which diode burned, and where was the short fixed?\n     - A photo of the glowing-points area.\n   - **Sources**:\n     - Planetary Pinball manual TOC: https://www.planetarypinball.com/reference/gamemanuals/The_Shadow_Bly/files/assets/basic-html/toc.html\n     - PinWiki schematic: https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/File:WPC_power_drive_board.pdf\n     - WPC theory 16-9289: https://planetarypinball.com/reference/partsmanuals/WMS_Schematic_WPC_16-9289/files/assets/seo/page32.html\n     - PinWiki The Shadow: https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/The_Shadow\n     - Leon Borre page: https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/Leon_Borre_Williams_WPC_and_WPC-95_Driver_Board_Repair\n     - PinWiki T2: https://pinwiki.com/wiki/index.php/Terminator_2:_Judgement_Day\n     - Marco 23-800: https://www.marcospecialties.com/pinball-parts/090-5001-00\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Send the French response described in section 8, giving the brief initial reasoning and only the first check (M1: isolation of J130-1 Violet-Brown to ground J116-3 and to earth, off-power with the PD disconnected, preceded by a DC voltage check), plus the open questions and sources. Then stop and wait, per the user's instruction: \"Présente brièvement ton raisonnement initial, puis guide-moi vers la première vérification sûre et pertinente. Attends mon résultat avant de continuer.\" After the user replies, record the result in `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (§4, §5 statuses, §8 next step) and give the next single measurement, likely the Sol 01 coil resistance J130-1 ↔ J107-2 compared with Sol 07 and Sol 08.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\vladi\\.claude\\projects\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"090141e4-4af0-4cc0-8245-c424805e87ed","timestamp":"2026-10-25T11:30:48.989Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":1,"turnIndex":1},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"golden-gathering-hearth"}
{"parentUuid":"090141e4-4af0-4cc0-8245-c424805e87ed","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\vladi\\.claude\\projects\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\memory\\shadow-diagnostic-method.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\vladi\\.claude\\projects\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\memory\\shadow-diagnostic-method.md","content":"---\nname: shadow-diagnostic-method\ndescription: \"How the user wants the Bally The Shadow pinball repair diagnosis run (one measurement at a time, journal file, challenge hypotheses)\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f\n  modified: 2026-10-25T10:35:47.132Z\n---\n\nFor the Bally The Shadow (1994, WPC-S) Power Driver diagnosis, guide exactly one manipulation or measurement per message (where, how, how to interpret), then wait for the result. Off-power checks first, account for charged capacitors, and never suggest powering on before the pre-reconnection checklist is done. Treat the user's recollections as uncertain, never as confirmed diagnoses, and contradict them when evidence requires. Answer in French.\n\n**Why:** the user asked for this explicitly; earlier unstructured measurements did not validate anything, and the Power Driver was already damaged several times.\n\n**How to apply:** start each session by reading `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (project root) and the `docs/` folder next to it (manual pages, A-12697 schematic); update the journal after each significant step (measurement table, hypothesis status, next step).\n","numLines":16,"startLine":1,"totalLines":16}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\Users\\vladi\\.claude\\projects\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\memory\\shadow-diagnostic-method.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"88e127ba-cadd-4fc4-9395-837706be2511","timestamp":"2026-10-25T11:30:49.191Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\vladi\\\\.claude\\\\projects\\\\C--sources-the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot\\\\memory\\\\shadow-diagnostic-method.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t---\n2\tname: shadow-diagnostic-method\n3\tdescription: \"How the user wants the Bally The Shadow pinball repair diagnosis run (one measurement at a time, journal file, challenge hypotheses)\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: feedback\n7\t  originSessionId: 67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f\n8\t  modified: 2026-10-25T10:35:47.132Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tFor the Bally The Shadow (1994, WPC-S) Power Driver diagnosis, guide exactly one manipulation or measurement per message (where, how, how to interpret), then wait for the result. Off-power checks first, account for charged capacitors, and never suggest powering on before the pre-reconnection checklist is done. Treat the user's recollections as uncertain, never as confirmed diagnoses, and contradict them when evidence requires. Answer in French.\n12\t\n13\t**Why:** the user asked for this explicitly; earlier unstructured measurements did not validate anything, and the Power Driver was already damaged several times.\n14\t\n15\t**How to apply:** start each session by reading `journal-diagnostic-the-shadow.md` (project root) and the `docs/` folder next to it (manual pages, A-12697 schematic); update the journal after each significant step (measurement table, hypothesis status, next step).\n16\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"C:\\sources\\the-shadow-pinball-troubleshoot","sessionId":"67a0b140-c89f-4ca5-be8f-b924fa2c867f","version":"2.1.310","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"golden-gathering-hearth"}
